      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Here is a protection most renters never claim. In most US states, if a landlord keeps any part of your deposit, they cannot just quietly take it. They have to send you an itemized statement. That means a written list, spelling out each deduction and what it was for, and often the receipts to back it up. A vague note saying cleaning and repairs is not enough.",
